    "title": "Venezuela earthquake interrupts baseball game as terrified players rush to safety - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Joseph McBride The Mirror US 1 hours ago 💬 0",
    "summary": "1 hours ago Professional baseball players were seen running for safety as two massive earthquakes struck central Venezuela on Wednesday. The Marineros were facing the Senadores in the Liga Mayor de Beisbol Profesional ( LMBP ), with the game hosted at Estadio Universitario in Caracas. At approximately 5:04 p.m. local time, back-to-back powerful earthquakes struck off the coast of Venezuela , causing widespread damage. The lack of cellphone signal in parts of Venezuela deepened the distress of many families, particularly those among the more than 7.7 million people who have left the country during its protracted crisis.",
